   "line": [
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": "He plays the Scotch — one of the oldest openings there is. Its idea is to contest the centre at once and open the bishop's diagonal."
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 32,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "exd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "We have to answer the central tension."
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 34.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "Nxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The downside of the Scotch: White has moved the same piece twice in the opening."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 47,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/2b5/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Bc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop to c5 develops while attacking his knight — developing with tempo, which is exactly what punishes moving a piece twice."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 52.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/2N5/2b5/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "Nxc6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
