   "line": [
    "Ne7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Developing the knight to e7 — and he can't castle: the bishop on c5 rakes into g1, and f3 just opened everything up. That's why strong players warn never to play f3."
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 114,
   "fen": "r1b1k2r/ppp1nppp/2p2q2/2b5/2B1PB2/5P2/PPP3PP/RN1QK2R b KQkq - 3 8",
   "line": [
    "Bf4"
   ],
   "spoken": "He plays the bishop to f4 — but the problem is he only sees that he's hitting a pawn; he misses my queen. This is tunnel vision, the source of most beginner mistakes."
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 125.5,
   "fen": "r1b1k2r/ppp1nppp/2p5/2b5/2B1Pq2/5P2/PPP3PP/RN1QK2R w KQkq - 0 9",
