   "line": [
    "Qe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Do we trade queens? Today's theme is converting a material advantage — and that starts here."
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 166,
   "fen": "r1b1k2r/ppp1nppp/2p5/2b1q3/2B1PP2/8/PPPQ2PP/RN2K2R b KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": "He plays f4 — and whenever a pawn moves, check what it left unprotected; a pawn push always leaves weaknesses in its wake."
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 187,
   "fen": "r1b1k2r/ppp1nppp/2p5/2b5/2B1PP2/8/PqPQ2PP/RN2K2R w KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Qxb2"
   ],
   "spoken": "It leaves both e4 and b2 loose. Qb2 is the better grab — it also attacks the rook on a1, which he can't save."
